 Lake\nTownships\nNew Dosey Township\nPokegama Township\nRoyalton Township\nWilma Township\nPine County Community Broadband Initiative\nHow Do I\nApply For\nEconomic Development\nEmployment\nChild Care License\nHomestead\nGun Permit\nMarriage License\nA Passport\nBuilding Permit\nSeptic Permits\neCRV\nWIC\nContact\nBoard of Commissioners\nCity Officials\nCounty Departments\nCourt Administration\nPhone Directory\nView\nAgendas and Minutes\nJail Roster\nComprehensive Plan\nBudget Book\nAbsentee Ballot Application\nPublic Health Alerts\nPlat Search\nTruth In Taxation\nLocal Government Officials Meeting\nOrdinances\nFind\nEconomic Development\nAdvertisement for Bids\nOffice Locations\nTax Forfeit Land Auction\nProperty Information\nElection Information\nRequest For Proposal\nPay\nProperty Taxes\nFines - MN Court\nProbation Fees\nReport an Issue\nslide 1 of 1\nQuick links\nHome\nNews List\nNews Post\nPress Release: Pine County Provides Statement Regarding Electronic Funds Transfer Investigation\nPRESS RELEASE\nPine County Provides Statement Regarding Electronic Funds Transfer Investigation\nPine City, Minn. (July 9, 2026): Pine County is investigating an electronic funds transfer\ninvolving a payment intended for a county vendor.\nThe payment, in the amount of $400,143.37, was intended for a public works contractor. Based\non information currently available, the payment appears to have been processed using\nfraudulent electronic payment instructions received through email as part of a suspected\nphishing scheme.\nUpon discovering the issue, the County immediately initiated its response and is working with\nthe appropriate financial institutions, law enforcement, and other relevant parties to determine\nhow the incident occurred, whether the funds can be recovered, and, if possible, identify the\nsource of the email that led to the payment. Multiple investigations remain ongoing.\nAt this time, the County has limited confirmed information and is allowing those investigative\nprocesses to proceed before drawing conclusions. The County recognizes the importance of\ntransparency and will provide additional information once the investigations have concluded.\nUntil then, any information beyond what has been released would be preliminary and\nunsubstantiated.\nFor media inquiries, please contact:\nKelly Schroeder\nCounty Administrator\nPine County\nKelly.Schroeder@pinecountymn.gov\n(320) 591-1620\nShare this page\n×\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.pinecountymn.gov/news_detail_T8_R227.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\nINFORMATION\nE-Notify\nOffice Locations\nContact Us\nFacebook Links\nEverbridge Notifications\nQUICK LINKS\nJail Roster\nBudget Book\nComprehensive Plan\nElection Information\nActive Warrants\nEmployees\nNews\nEvent Calendar\nContact Us\nContact Us\n-->\n635 Northridge Drive NW, Pine City MN 55063\n(320)591-1400\nContact Information\nPowered by revize. Government Website Experts | Login | 635 Northridge Drive NW, Pine City MN 55063 - Questions? (320)591-1400\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate\nClose Read More",
